# FPGA Image Enhancement using Quantized Residual CNN

> FPGA-accelerated image enhancement pipeline using Quantization-Aware Residual CNNs, INT8 optimization, and Vitis AI deployment for efficient real-time inference.

---

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10-blue)
![FPGA](https://img.shields.io/badge/Hardware-FPGA-green)
![Vitis AI](https://img.shields.io/badge/Vitis-AI-orange)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-red)

---

# Overview

This project presents an FPGA-based image enhancement system built using Residual Convolutional Neural Networks (Residual CNNs) with INT8 quantization for hardware-efficient deployment.

The pipeline is optimized for:

- Image restoration
- Noise reduction
- Low-light enhancement
- Blur correction
- FPGA real-time inference acceleration

The deployment workflow uses:

- PyTorch training
- Quantization-aware optimization
- Vitis AI compilation
- FPGA DPU inference execution

The system is designed to preserve enhancement quality while achieving efficient low-precision inference on FPGA hardware platforms.

---

# Features

- Residual CNN image enhancement architecture
- INT8 quantized inference pipeline
- FPGA-oriented deployment workflow
- Vitis AI integration
- DPU hardware acceleration
- Docker-based reproducible environment
- PSNR / SSIM evaluation pipeline
- Runtime benchmarking support
- FPGA-compatible `.xmodel` deployment
- Hardware-software co-design workflow

---

# System Architecture

```text
Dataset
   ↓
Residual CNN
   ↓
Quantization-Aware Training
   ↓
INT8 Optimization
   ↓
XModel Generation
   ↓
DPU Compilation
   ↓
FPGA Inference
   ↓
Enhanced Output
```

