---

# Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/FPGA-Image-Enhancement.git
cd FPGA-Image-Enhancement
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# Software Inference

The software inference workflow automatically:

- Loads the trained Residual CNN model
- Processes degraded input images
- Generates enhanced outputs
- Creates output directories automatically

### Input Directory

```bash
testing_images/degraded/
```

### Output Directory

```bash
output/
```

### Software Model

```bash
models/best_model_arch1.pth
```

### Run Inference

```bash
python testing_code/test.py
```

---

# FPGA Deployment

The repository also includes the FPGA deployment model:

```bash
models/model_b8_c128_int.xmodel
```

The `.xmodel` artifact was generated using the Vitis AI quantization and compilation workflow for FPGA-oriented DPU execution.

## Supported Deployment Workflow

- USB-based deployment
- PuTTY runtime execution
- FPGA DPU inference
- Runtime FPS benchmarking
- Hardware acceleration evaluation

Detailed deployment instructions are available in:

```bash
docs/
```

---

# Docker Support

A Docker-based execution environment is included for reproducible inference workflows.

### Docker Setup

```bash
docker build -t fpga-enhancement .
docker run -it fpga-enhancement
```

Additional setup instructions:

```bash
docs/SOFTWARE_SETUP.md
```

